{start_of_verse}
Well, I heard you died out in [Em]Cheyenne
With my mother's ring on your [C]hand
A note in your pocket said "I'll love you till I [G]die" [D]
I can hear the bulls are coming to claim that they've been [Em]hunting
The son of the cowboy came to claim his [C]daddy's right
And my baby she's been crying at the thought of me [G]dying [D]
She knows there's no stopping a man and his foolish pride
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
So [C]open the gates, I'm here to [G]prove
I'm better than my father [D]was and where he came from [Em]too
So [C]open the gates, I'm here to [G]ride
To hell I'll [D]go with daddy by my [Em]side
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_instrumental}
| [Em] | [C] | [G] | [D] |
{end_of_instrumental}

{start_of_verse}
And I ain't never feared nothing that was four-legged and [Em]bucking
Throw me on a hurricane and I'll [C]ride it to the coast
You'll never know that your son came to do what you should've [G]done [D]
On a summer day a long time ago, top a bull named To Hell I Go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
